Headset Desk @VERSION@ - Windows 11 x64

Run headset-desk.exe from this folder. Keep all DLL, plugin and license files.
Pair WH-1000XM5 or WH-CH720N using Windows Bluetooth settings, then turn it on.
Choose Connect if the app did not connect automatically.

Changing settings is experimental and starts off. Turn on "Experimental controls"
under Noise control to change Noise Cancelling, Ambient (1-20), Off, the five EQ
bands and Clear Bass. EQ edits stay local until Apply; Reset discards them.
Each change is sent once and checked with a fresh readback. A failure turns the
controls off; reconnecting never replays a setting. No firmware updates or power
commands are offered.

Close hides to the tray; tray Quit exits. The application runs offline. No Qt
installation, account or startup entry is needed. This build is unsigned, and
Windows SmartScreen may warn about an unrecognized application.

Source, installer, releases, checksums and issue tracker:
https://github.com/ashwinpr15/headset-desk

Qt and runtime licenses are in licenses/. Exact corresponding Qt sources:
https://github.com/ashwinpr15/headset-desk/releases/download/v@VERSION@/headset-desk-v@VERSION@-qt-runtime-sources.zip
